  "important": [
    {
      "date": "2025-09-26T15:23:19",
      "from": "Argon",
      "text": "da teq shoulders sa nekva greshka"
    },
    {
      "date": "2025-10-17T11:57:51",
      "from": "Argon",
      "text": "най важното е добрите приятели, които са в тези коли ❤️"
    },
    {
      "date": "2025-11-05T12:08:26",
      "from": "Argon",
      "text": "ANATOMY OF NUTRA VSLs – How to make VSLs for supplements & beauty products that actually work\n\ndisclaimer: this won’t work for gadgets, but it will for any serum, cream, powder, etc.\n\none of the biggest mistakes brands make is showing the product in the beginning of the VSL\n\n…and then they go on to talk about its ingredients and the compounds and whatever else fixes the problem\n\nwhat you should instead do is start off by presenting the unique mechanism of the problem (which is the root cause)\n\nthen you get into the unique mechanism of the solution itself (MAKE THIS COMPELLING)\n\naka the unique solution to the root cause\n\nand then that UMS consists of certain compounds that activate\n\nhere’s an example of what i mean from another VSL:\n\nhook: “you need to switch on your caloric bypass”\n\nthen they go on about the certain ingredients that activate the caloric bypass so you can lose weight\n\nand since they go deep into the science they’ll give it some braindead science name like “cell repairers” or “meta boosters”\n\nthose compounds are framed as something that’s “exotic” which you couldn’t find on Amazon or just some grocery shop\n\nyour goal is to coin an “exotic” name like that for the compounds in your product"
